          %p
            Given a unital ring (or only a monoid)
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and a
            %strong central
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+subset"} multiplicative subset
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\subset Z(R)\subset R
            (i.e. set containing
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\in R
            and with every two elements containing their product, and such that all its elements are central in
            = succeed ")" do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1} R
            is sometimes said to be the
            %strong commutative localization
            of
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            at
            = succeed ";" do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\to S^{-1} R
            of rings (monoids resp.). The ring of fractions is defined as the set of equivalence classes
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,r)\in S\times R
            where
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∼
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,r)\sim (t,r')
            iff
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists u\in S
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mi s
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mi u
                  %mi t
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u s r' = u t r
            (if
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
            one can skip mentioning
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            in this condition); the equivalence classes are called fractions and denoted
            = succeed ";" do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^{-1}r
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            it is easy to guess the multiplication rule
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mi s
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^{-1}r t^{-1} r' = (t s)^{-1} (r r')
            and for the addition one first takes the representatives with the same denominator and then adds the numerators. E.g. the formula
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mi s
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mi r
                  %mo +
                  %mi s
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^{-1}r + t^{-1}r' = (t s)^{-1} (t r + s r')
            will do, and we indeed get a ring
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1} R
            with unit
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1^{-1} 1
            together with the canonical homomorphism of rings
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\to S^{-1} R
            given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\mapsto 1^{-1} r
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Localization+of+commutative+rings"} Localization of commutative rings
            at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+subsets"} multiplicative subsets
            is the standard example, but the centrality of
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is enough for the whole theory to pass through.
          %p Commutative localization can be extended to left modules.
          %p
            %strong Module of fractions
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1} M
            is the left
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1} R
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1} M
            equipped with the natural map of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\to S^{-1}M
            and defined as follows:
          %p
            The underlying set of
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1} M
            consists of equivalence classes
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^{-1} m
            of pairs
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,m)\in S\times M
            where
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,m)\cong (t,n)
            iff there exist
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\in S
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mi t
                    %mi m
                    %mo =
                    %mi u
                    %mi s
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u t m = u s n
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mi s
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s^{-1} r)(t^{-1} m):= (t s)^{-1} (r m)
            and the addition is
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_36.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi m
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mi t
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mi m
                    %mo +
                    %mi s
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^{-1} m + t^{-1} n := (s t)^{-1}(t m + s n)
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_37.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_S : M\mapsto S^{-1} M
            extends to a functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_38.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_R Mod\to {}_{S^{-1} R}Mod
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_39.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: {}_{S^{-1} R}Mod \to {}_R Mod
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
            and there is a natural transformation of functors
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_40.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Id
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id\to U Q_S
            whose components are the
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_41.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_42.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\to S^{-1}M
            given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\mapsto 1^{-1}m
          %p
            It can be then shown that this elementary approach is equivalent to the definition via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
            formula
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi M
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1}M = S^{-1} R\otimes_R M
          %p
            The basic result is that the commutative localization
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1} R
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+module"} flat
            left module over
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ore+localization"} Ore localization
          %p
            Commutative localization in which also
            %math#mathml_ddcfc7732a60e702d8e832e02cb350411562e29c_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is commutative is a basic procedure used in defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+scheme"} algebraic scheme
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+space"} locally ringed space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+field"} quotient field
            of a commutative
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
